<!-- 
    templates_latex/ — Jinja2 templates that render to LaTeX (.tex), NOT HTML.

    WHY A SEPARATE FOLDER?
    Flask auto-discovers templates in templates/ and treats them as HTML.
    Our LaTeX templates use the same Jinja2 syntax ({{ }}, {% %}) but
    produce .tex files, not HTML.  Keeping them in a different folder:
      1. Prevents Flask from accidentally serving them as web pages.
      2. Makes it clear to developers which templates produce HTML
         vs. which produce LaTeX.
      3. Lets us use a standalone Jinja2 Environment with custom
         delimiters (LaTeX uses { } heavily, so we may switch Jinja2
         to use (( )) or similar to avoid clashes).

    This file is a placeholder so Git tracks the empty directory.
-->
